d:“Why frame a clearing when the ruins are right here?”
“Because anyone can take a picture of what they are looking at. I wanted a picture from where I stood.”
“So the true attraction is at your back?”
“Exactly. What mattered wasn't in front of the lens.”

They christened this sanctuary for a faith it never served, mistaking primordial megaliths for a house of prayer. Time preserved the lie in its name, but the mountain remembers.

Find where the observer stood. Look away from the clearing.
